  "body": "Hub (PathPilot v2.14.4) lists the **1300PL**, a CNC **plasma** table. Unlike the mills, lathes and routers, it is not just a machine file: CamCraft has no plasma capability today.\n\n**Open questions (research first, no code):**\n1. **Operation:** a 2D profile op that cuts *through*, with no depth stepping. Lead-ins and lead-outs suited to plasma, kerf compensation (the kerf width as the tool \"diameter\") and the inside/outside side rule.\n2. **Torch control:** torch on/off words in PathPilot's plasma dialect, pierce height and pierce delay, cut height, and torch height control (THC) on/off around tight corners and holes.\n3. **Machine kind:** a plasma kind in the `.mch`, with no spindle rpm, no Z-depth cutting and a Z used for torch height, plus how the machine check and stock sim treat it (the stock sim's material model doesn't fit a through-cut).\n4. **Post:** a PathPilot plasma post, and whether PathPilot plasma differs from the mill dialect beyond the torch words.\n5. **Safety laws:** what replaces the gouge and collision checks (torch height and part tip-up are the real hazards).\n\n**Next step:** answer these from Tormach's 1300PL manual (the contributor can supply it) and public LinuxCNC plasma docs, then file concrete sub-issues per the needs-research process.\n\nRelated: the Hub machine coverage issues filed alongside (770M+/1100M+, 15LX, routers), and #611 and #612.",
